## Proof

**Setup.** Label the canisters R₁, R₂ (Red), W₁, W₂ (White), B₁, B₂ (Blue). Within each color pair, exactly one is Heavy (weight H) and one is Light (weight L), with H > L. A configuration is a triple (r, w, b) where r ∈ {1, 2} means R_r is Heavy, etc. There are 2³ = 8 configurations.

**Lower bound: 1 weighing is insufficient.** A single balance-scale weighing has 3 possible outcomes (left heavier, balanced, right heavier). Since 3 < 8, one weighing cannot distinguish all 8 configurations. So at least 2 weighings are required.

**Upper bound: 2 weighings suffice.** We give an adaptive strategy.

**Weighing 1:** Place R₁ + W₁ on the left pan, R₂ + B₁ on the right pan.

Computing the left-minus-right weight difference for each configuration:

| Config (r,w,b) | Left = wt(R₁)+wt(W₁) | Right = wt(R₂)+wt(B₁) | Difference | Outcome |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| (1,1,1) | 2H | L+H | H−L > 0 | Left > Right |
| (1,1,2) | 2H | 2L | 2(H−L) > 0 | Left > Right |
| (1,2,1) | H+L | L+H | 0 | Balanced |
| (1,2,2) | H+L | 2L | H−L > 0 | Left > Right |
| (2,1,1) | L+H | 2H | −(H−L) < 0 | Left < Right |
| (2,1,2) | L+H | H+L | 0 | Balanced |
| (2,2,1) | 2L | 2H | −2(H−L) < 0 | Left < Right |
| (2,2,2) | 2L | H+L | −(H−L) < 0 | Left < Right |

This partitions the 8 configurations into three groups:
- **Left > Right:** (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,2) — 3 configs
- **Balanced:** (1,2,1), (2,1,2) — 2 configs
- **Left < Right:** (2,1,1), (2,2,1), (2,2,2) — 3 configs

**Weighing 2 (adaptive):**

**Case A — Weighing 1 gave Left > Right** (configs (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,2); in all, R₁ is Heavy). Weigh **W₁ vs B₂**:

| Config | W₁ | B₂ | Outcome |
|---|---|---|---|
| (1,1,1) | H | L | Left > Right |
| (1,1,2) | H | H | Balanced |
| (1,2,2) | L | H | Left < Right |

Three distinct outcomes → configuration fully identified.

**Case B — Weighing 1 gave Balanced** (configs (1,2,1), (2,1,2)). Weigh **R₁ vs W₁**:

| Config | R₁ | W₁ | Outcome |
|---|---|---|---|
| (1,2,1) | H | L | Left > Right |
| (2,1,2) | L | H | Left < Right |

Two distinct outcomes → configuration fully identified.

**Case C — Weighing 1 gave Left < Right** (configs (2,1,1), (2,2,1), (2,2,2); in all, R₂ is Heavy, so R₁ is Light). Weigh **W₁ vs B₂**:

| Config | W₁ | B₂ | Outcome |
|---|---|---|---|
| (2,1,1) | H | L | Left > Right |
| (2,2,1) | L | L | Balanced |
| (2,2,2) | L | H | Left < Right |

Three distinct outcomes → configuration fully identified.

**Conclusion.** Every one of the 8 configurations yields a unique pair of outcomes across the two weighings, so 2 weighings always identify all three Heavy-Metal canisters. Since 1 weighing is provably insufficient, the minimum number of weighings required is:

**2**

